# Database Configuration for ClientFlow Tracker
# Default is local SQLite (tracker.db).
# To connect to PostgreSQL & manage with pgAdmin, set DATABASE_URL below:

# PostgreSQL Connection String Format:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<username>:<password>@<host>:<port>/<database_name>
# Example:
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/tracker_db

# How to manage with pgAdmin:
# 1. Open pgAdmin 4.
# 2. Right click "Servers" -> "Register" -> "Server...".
# 3. In "General", name it "ClientFlow Tracker DB".
# 4. In "Connection":
#    - Host name/address: localhost (or 127.0.0.1)
#    - Port: 5433 (PostgreSQL 18 is running on port 5433)
#    - Maintenance database: postgres
#    - Username: postgres
#    - Password: <your-postgres-password>

# 5. Click Save. You will see the tables: "clients", "followups", "notifications".
